# 🤖 FORGE SDK 2D - AI AGENT RULES

Before modifying any code, proposing refactors, or writing new files, you MUST comply with these instructions:

1. **Read Guidelines First:** You MUST read [doc/AI_GUIDELINES.md](file:///c:/Users/xico0/Desktop/Xico/doc/AI_GUIDELINES.md) and [doc/README.md](file:///c:/Users/xico0/Desktop/Xico/doc/README.md) before proposing or implementing changes.
2. **Obey Workspace Rules:** Acatar las reglas de agentes descritas en [.agents/AGENTS.md](file:///c:/Users/xico0/Desktop/Xico/.agents/AGENTS.md).
3. **No Duplicate Files:** Under NO circumstances should you create new documentation files in `doc/tools/` unless they are explicitly authorized in [doc/TOOLS.md](file:///c:/Users/xico0/Desktop/Xico/doc/TOOLS.md). Individual `.md` files for unit tests, secondary UI components, or auxiliary helper modules are strictly prohibited. Document all new tests in `doc/tools/TESTS.md`, all new UIs in `doc/tools/Uis.md`, and catalog minor utilities in Section 3 of their corresponding main tool's document. Loose task list files (such as `todo.md`) in the workspace root are strictly prohibited; document plans/tasks only in [doc/PROGRESO.md](file:///c:/Users/xico0/Desktop/Xico/doc/PROGRESO.md). Logic updates, integrations, synchronizations, or cross-cutting queries must be documented by updating the existing corresponding tool documents, never by creating new integration docs. If a new tool doc is authorized, create it named after its exact usage using the 10-section template. Markdown files must not exceed 1,500-3,000 lines; if a document grows too large, logically split it (e.g. `_PART2.md` or `_HISTORY.md`). Each time a significant `.md` file is created or edited, you MUST generate or update a Table of Contents (Index) header at the top of the file to enable surgical partial reads. Always edit the original file for changes to pre-existing features.
4. **Surgical Edits Only:** Perform surgical edits using partial replacements rather than rewriting complete documentation files.
5. **Path Tolerance:** If files or directories have been refactored, perform recursive searches (grep/find) rather than assuming they don't exist.
6. **Detailed Functions Catalog:** Register all new public Rust structures or functions in Section 3 of their corresponding tool markdown files.
7. **Style Consistency:** Prioritize and maintain the existing code structure, formatting, style, and patterns of the files you edit. Do NOT perform full-file reformats or rewrite logic in different styles (e.g., changing error handling, control flows, or borrowing models) unless explicitly requested. New code must blend seamlessly with the surrounding code.
8. **Automatic Handoff (Progress Update):** At the end of every task or session, you MUST update [doc/PROGRESO.md](file:///c:/Users/xico0/Desktop/Xico/doc/PROGRESO.md) with details of your work, updated tests count (currently 96 total), and define the next goals clearly under "🎯 PRÓXIMOS OBJETIVOS" so the next AI agent can resume without friction.
